834	     * Rolls a registration date forward onto a business day. A date that already falls on a
835	     * weekday which is not a public holiday is returned unchanged; a Saturday, Sunday or listed
836	     * public holiday is rolled forward, one day at a time, until the next non-weekend,
837	     * non-holiday day is reached. This adjusted date is what gets stored as the
838	     * {@code registrationDate} and drives everything derived from it (the fiscal year, the
839	     * membership number's fiscal-year segment, the daily create-limit).
840	     *
841	     * @param date the effective registration date (supplied by the client or defaulted to the
842	     *             server's current date)
843	     * @return the same date if it is a business day, otherwise the next business day that is
844	     *         neither a weekend nor a public holiday
845	     */
846	    private static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
847	        while (isNonBusinessDay(date)) {
848	            date = date.plusDays(1);
849	        }
850	        return date;
851	    }
